---
import data from '@site/instruments/data/ipip-neo-120.json';
import normsData from '@site/instruments/data/norms/ipip-neo-120.json';
import TestPage from '../../../layouts/TestPage.astro';
import { bigFive } from '../../../tests/big-five';

---

<TestPage content={bigFive} data={data} normsData={normsData}>
	<p slot="intro">The Big Five are the five broad traits that personality research keeps finding: neuroticism, extraversion, openness, agreeableness and conscientiousness. This inventory measures each with six facets, so it can say not just how extraverted you are but whether that comes from warmth, sociability, assertiveness, pace, thrill-seeking or cheerfulness. It is the public-domain IPIP-NEO-120, scored on your device and compared with a sample of over 400,000 people.</p>
	<Fragment slot="limits">
		<p>Limits worth knowing: this is a self-report, so it measures how you see yourself. Four-item facets are short, and several have alphas below 0.70, so a facet score moves more between attempts than a domain score does. The comparison sample answered online, is young on average, and is not a representative sample of any country.</p>
	</Fragment>
</TestPage>
